    <p>
      This site is an independent hobby project listing APIs I maintain myself.
      It isn't affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by GitHub or the Go
      module proxy (pkg.go.dev) — any product names, logos, and brands mentioned
      are the property of their respective owners.
    </p>
    <p>
      The links here (repos, OpenAPI specs, SDK docs) point at the actual source
      of truth for each API and are kept up to date on a best-effort basis, but
      this page itself can lag the repos it links to — the repo is always the
      authority, not this catalogue.
    </p>
